# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 132's class, lane recovery-b4, beside
# `fixedbugs-132-a-backslash-joins-its-line-to-the-next`. Symptom: the line a
# `\` asked for went as a block no head opens, and its own mistake with it,
# the `)` below never told. Now the line is joined and read, so its mistake
# is told beside the `\`'s one message. And a `\` after an operator at the
# file's end joins nothing: the line is ended there, and what it lacks is
# told in the parser's words. The certain fixes join the first and delete the
# second `\`, and the program keeps the two mistakes no fix repairs.

function a_mistake_on_the_line_it_joins()
    #~v unexpected_character
    x = 1 + 2 )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    print(x)

function at_the_files_end_after_an_operator()
    x = 1 +  #~ unexpected_character #~v expected_expression
